    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d971">

                <pb facs="1146" n="1036" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg1036"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Contractual Obligations/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-12T15:00:00+08:00">January 12, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 12—8:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Department’s 9, January 10, 5 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d971-f1"/> I consider
                    that it would not be premature to request statements from American creditors. It
                    is my understanding that until statements are prepared I can go no further with
                    the Minister of Finance on this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
